sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Programs that share CUDA with OpenGL, and NVIDIA's control panel, keep
    NVIDIA's own OpenGL when the session runs OpenGL on zink: their menu
    entries and their names in a terminal start through
    sparky-stereo-nvidia-opengl. The list starts with DaVinci Resolve and
    nvidia-settings; /etc/sparky-stereo/opengl-programs and the person's
    ~/.config/sparky-stereo/opengl-programs add a program ("NAME nvidia")
    or give one back to zink ("NAME zink"), and the person's choice wins.

